    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n468" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγερ-μός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>collection of money for the service
				of the gods</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγείρω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1015.27
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Halicarnassus</span>), <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.19
			</span></i> (with v. l. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγυρμός</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				8.360d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.111
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the call-to-arms</i> of the Greeks against Troy, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1451a27
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> metaph.,
				<i>collection</i>, of wisdom and experience, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				4.20
			</span></i>.</div>
